# Karpathy guidelines

- State assumptions before editing. If a series is missing, leave it blank.
- Touch only the files the task needs.
- Prefer a library that already does the job. Write new code when no library covers the case.
- Every behavior that changes a number has a failing test first, then the code that makes it pass.
- Do not invent a weight, a primary balance, or a yield.
